From b4b875a330f69d60627f89f2dae667bf055ac8db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:36:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] service: don't leak the Transaction-ID of a retrieved message

result_request_retrieve_conf() replaced the Transaction-ID that
mms_message_decode() had just decoded from the M-Retrieve.conf with
the one of the notification, without freeing it, for every message
mmsd retrieved. LeakSanitizer found it in an end-to-end test.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/service.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/service.c b/src/service.c
index daea428..409a56a 100644
--- a/src/service.c
+++ b/src/service.c
@@ -3440,6 +3440,7 @@ result_request_retrieve_conf (struct mms_request *request)
 
   decode_success = mms_message_decode (pdu, len, msg);
 
+  g_free (msg->transaction_id);
   msg->transaction_id = g_strdup (request->msg->transaction_id);
 
   if (decode_success == TRUE)
-- 
2.53.0

